    "content": "# Summary\n\nIn this session, you explored the complete Physical AI workflow that will be used throughout this course.\n\nIn the following module, you were introduced to building your robot lab to complete a pick-and-place task. You also learned about the LeRobot ecosystem, the role of community datasets, and how modern robot learning pipelines integrate data collection, training, deployment, and evaluation.\n\nWe also briefly discussed the concept of sim-to-real transfer and why simulation has become a critical tool for scaling robot learning. Finally, you became familiar with the reBot Arm B601 RS platform, which will serve as the hardware foundation for all upcoming experiments.\n\nNow that you understand the overall workflow, it's time to prepare the physical system.\n\nIn the next chapter, **Build Your Robot Lab**, you will assemble and configure the hardware environment, verify robot connectivity, and prepare the workspace for data collection and policy training.\n"
